.TH BACKLIGHT 1 blight\-@VERSION@
.SH NAME
blight \- read and adjust display backlight
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B blight
.RB [ option ]
.RB [ operation ]
.RB [ value... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.P
Simple and minimal program to adjust screen backlight and get the current
backlight level.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B "\-h, \-\-help, \-help, help, h"
Print brief usage information to standard output and exit.

.TP
.B "\-v, \-\-verbose, \-verbose, verbose, v"
Show verbose output.

.TP
.B "\-d, \-\-debug, \-debug, debug, d"
Show debug output.

.SH OPERATIONS
.TP
.B "get, g"
Get current brightness value. Return value is in the 0 to 255 INT range.

.TP
.B "set, s"
Set brightness value. The value can be in the 0 to 255 INT range, larger values
are capped to 255, negatives are capped to 0, INT percentages from 0 to 100 are
also accepted, the
.B "+"
plus and
.B "-"
minus signs are accepted as modifier argument after the value to change the
operation to either increase or decrease by the value amount.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Get current brightness:
.RS
blight g
.RE
Example output:
.RS
255
.RE

.TP
Get current brightness with debug output:
.RS
blight d g
.RE
Example output:
.RS
Operation: get
.br
255 (100%)
.RE

.TP
Set brightness to 255:
.RS
blight g 255
.RE

.TP
Set brightness to 100%:
.RS
blight g 100%
.RE

.TP
Set brightness to 255 with debug output:
.RS
blight d g 255
.RE
Example output:
.RS
Operation: set
.br
    value: 255
.br
brightness level: 255 (100%)  amdgpu_bl0 [actual value:    255]
.RE

.TP
Set brightness to 100% with debug output:
.RS
blight d g 100%
.RE
Example output:
.RS
Operation: set
.br
    value: 255
.br
brightness level: 255 (100%)  amdgpu_bl0 [actual value:    255]
.RE

.TP
Try to set brightness to 500 with debug output:
.RS
blight d g 500
.RE
Example output:
.RS
Operation: set
.br
    value: 500
.br
brightness level: 255 (100%)  amdgpu_bl0 [actual value:    255]
.RE

.TP
Increase brightness by 5:
.RS
blight s 5 +
.RE

.TP
Increase brightness by 5%:
.RS
blight s 5% +
.RE

